From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid Komarianskyi <leonid_komarianskyi@epam.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 11:43:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] xen-mapcache: adjust bucket size

Due to the nature of the xen-mapcache algorithms and virtio protocols,
using large bucket sizes leads to insufficient performance, especially
for virtio-blk. Each I/O operation using virtio requires several to tens
of map/unmap operations. Synthetic tests show that the average map/unmap
speed for foreign memory is approximately 300-350 MB/s. This means that
with a bucket size of 1 MB (the default shift of 20 bits), each map and
unmap operation takes about 3 to 10 ms. Considering this is pure delay -
and that, in addition, QEMU must process other operations and
synchronize them - the total I/O throughput may decrease to as low as
3-4 MB/s.

Therefore, reducing the bucket size decreases the overhead for map/unmap
operations on small buffers that were not previously mapped by mapcache,
resulting in increased total I/O bandwidth. Setting the bucket size to
16 bits (64 KB) is optimal, as making it smaller would increase overhead
from ioctl calls.

(cherry picked from commit 0bafd78991825f7d5f167d0591684fc5835ca593)

Signed-off-by: Leonid Komarianskyi <leonid_komarianskyi@epam.com>
Reviewed-by: Dmytro Firsov <dmytro_firsov@epam.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream fork / BSP-layer delta; not submitted upstream]
Origin: https://github.com/xen-troops/qemu commit 0bafd78991825f7d5f167d0591684fc5835ca593
---
 hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c | 10 +++-------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c b/hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c
index 6cd5b16c5..51334a27e 100644
--- a/hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c
+++ b/hw/xen/xen-mapcache.c
@@ -139,11 +139,13 @@ static MapCache *xen_map_cache_init_single(phys_offset_to_gaddr_t f,
     return mc;
 }
 
+#define DEFAULT_BUCKET_SHIFT 16U
+
 void xen_map_cache_init(phys_offset_to_gaddr_t f, void *opaque)
 {
     struct rlimit rlimit_as;
     unsigned long max_mcache_size;
-    unsigned int bucket_shift;
+    unsigned int bucket_shift = DEFAULT_BUCKET_SHIFT;
 
     xen_region_gnttabdev = xengnttab_open(NULL, 0);
     if (xen_region_gnttabdev == NULL) {
@@ -151,12 +153,6 @@ void xen_map_cache_init(phys_offset_to_gaddr_t f, void *opaque)
         exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
     }
 
-    if (HOST_LONG_BITS == 32) {
-        bucket_shift = 16;
-    } else {
-        bucket_shift = 20;
-    }
-
     if (geteuid() == 0) {
         rlimit_as.rlim_cur = RLIM_INFINITY;
         rlimit_as.rlim_max = RLIM_INFINITY;
